  "$comment": "languages-world-2 (11 November 2026): the WhatsApp allergen guard’s trigger words for HINDI (hi-IN): एलर्जी / एलर्जिक (and ऐलर्जी, अलर्जी), असहिष्णुता / इनटॉलरेंस, सीलिएक, ग्लूटेन फ्री / मुक्त, बिना <allergen> / <allergen> के बिना / <allergen> नहीं, नहीं खा सकता/सकती, पचता नहीं / हजम नहीं, परहेज, सुरक्षित, उपयुक्त, कंटैमिनेशन / संदूषण, अंश हो सकते — plus romanised Hindi (allergy hai, bina doodh, nahi kha sakta). Vowel signs, virama, anusvara and nukta are stripped on both sides, so every stem is checked by its consonant skeleton: bare बिना (→ बन, inside बना / बने / बन) and bare मुक्त are NOT stems, and एलर्ज is not matched by लार्ज (large); बिना तिल is left out (→ the skeleton of बना तला, made fried). OPTION B, as every other language: absence / safety words only, NOT the bare allergen names (a presence question may reach the AI, which answers only from the tags and gets the caveat). Matched with the Unicode normaliser. caveatWords: a tagged label of the codex allergen set (stored in English, lower case) → the words a reply may use for it (matched on the raw lower-cased reply, so written as the AI writes them). The country has no allergen set of its own yet, so caveatWords are for 'codex' (as MX, SG, HK, MY, TH and AE).",
